{"id":"bd_49Agents-jt4.14","title":"Placement mode cannot complete on a touch device","description":"Creating any pane enters placement mode (src-client/modules/placement.js:58), which positions the ghost from mousemove and commits on a canvas-container click. A touch device produces neither: there is no mousemove before the tap, so snappedX/snappedY are never set, and the tap does not arrive as the click the handler expects.

The practical effect is that the add-pane menu opens and the ghost appears, but no pane can be created by touch. Confirmed under Playwright device emulation, where the add -> note -> tap-canvas sequence leaves state.panes empty; the e2e suite has to seed panes through window.TC2_DEBUG as a result.

This makes it the most severe mobile gap found so far: the app cannot be used to create anything on a phone.","acceptance_criteria":"Tapping the canvas in placement mode creates the pane at the tapped position on a touch device, with a sensible position when no hover has occurred. Covered by an e2e spec under device emulation that drives the real add-pane flow.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"myradism@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-08-19T21:31:36Z","created_by":"MYRADhub","updated_at":"2026-08-19T21:31:36Z"}
